@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# Przed testami: pnpm migrate:latest && pnpm seed:run   (id 1-6: admin + 5 użytkowników z rezerwacjami)
# Równoległe rejestracje: pnpm register-race 10

### 1. Rejestracja -> 201, email znormalizowany do małych liter, rola USER, bez hasha
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "Tomasz.Lewandowski@example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo"
}

### 2. Duplikat różniący się wielkością liter (i spacjami) -> 409 EMAIL_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "  TOMASZ.LEWANDOWSKI@EXAMPLE.COM ",
  "password": "inne-dlugie-haslo"
}

### 3. Próba nadania roli ADMIN -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (Unrecognized key: "role")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hacker@example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 4. Inne nieznane pole -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ewa@example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo",
  "passwordHash": "$2b$12$..."
}

### 5. Za krótkie hasło (9 znaków) -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ewa@example.com",
  "password": "123456789"
}

### 6. Za długie hasło (73 znaki) -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ewa@example.com",
  "password": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
}

### 7. 40 znaków, ale 80 bajtów UTF-8 (limit bcrypt to 72 bajty) -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ewa@example.com",
  "password": "ąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąąą"
}

### 8. Niepoprawny email i brak hasła -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (2 błędy w details)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "to-nie-jest-email"
}

### 9. Email admina z seeda -> 409 EMAIL_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "Admin@Example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo"
}
